          %h3#of_line_bundles Of line bundles
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+characteristic+class"}> canonical characteristic class
              ,
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Theta+characteristic"} Theta characteristic
          %h3#of_linear_representations Of linear representations
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+class+of+a+linear+representation"} characteristic class of a linear representation
          %h3#chern_character Chern character
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern+character"} Chern character
            is a natural characteristic class with values in real cohomology. See there for more details.
          %h3#invariants
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            \-Invariants
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/k-invariants"} k-invariants
          %h3#level_in_chernsimons_theory
            Level in
            = succeed "-Chern-Simons" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/level+%28Chern-Simons+theory%29"} level (Chern-Simons theory)
          %h3#of_lagrangian_submanifolds Of Lagrangian submanifolds
          %p
            A characteristic class of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+submanifolds"} Lagrangian submanifolds
            is the
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maslov+index"} Maslov index
          %h3#classes_in_the_sense_of_fuks Classes in the sense of Fuks
          %p
            In (
            %a{:href => "#Fuks"}> Fuks (1987), section 7
            ) an axiomatization of characteristic classes is proposed. We review the definition and discuss how it is a special case of the one given above.
          %h4#fukss_definition Fuks’s definition
          %p
            Fuks considers a base category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T}
            of “spaces” and a category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒮
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}
            of spaces with a structure (for example, space together with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
            on it), this category should be a category over
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo :
                    %mi 𝒮
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U : \mathcal{S}\to\mathcal{T}
          %p
            A morphism of categories with structures is a morphism in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/overcategory"} overcategory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi 𝒯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} /\mathcal{T}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo →
                  %mi U
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\to U'
            is a functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo :
                  %mi dom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi dom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F: dom(U)\to dom(U')
            such that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ′
                    %mi F
                    %mo =
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U' F = U
          %p
            Suppose now the category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T}
            is equipped with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+theory"} cohomology theory
            which is, for purposes of this definition, a functor of the form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝒯
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H : \mathcal{T}^{op} \to A
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is some
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+category"} concrete category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+over+an+algebraic+theory"} T-algebras
            for some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+theory"} algebraic theory
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℋ
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi ℋ
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{H} = \mathcal{H}_H
            as a category whose objects are pairs
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,a)
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a space (= object in
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T}
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a\in H(X)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+category"} concrete category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,a)\to (Y,b)
            is a morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: X\to Y
            such that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H(f)(b) = a
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mo =
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^* = H(f)
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*(b) = a
          %p
            A
            %strong
              characteristic class of structures of type
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒮
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}
              with values in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            in the sense of (
            %a{:href => "#Fuks"}> Fuks
            ) is a morphism of structures
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi h
                  %mo :
                  %mi 𝒮
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi ℋ
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h: \mathcal{S}\to\mathcal{H}_H
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            of the type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒮
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}
            over a space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T}
            it assigns an element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi h
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h(S)
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H(X)
            such that for a morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi t
                  %mo :
                  %mi S
                  %mo →
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t: S\to T
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒮
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}
            the homomorphism
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo *
                    %mo :
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (U(t))^* : H(Y)\to H(X)
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                    %mo =
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y = U(T)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi h
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h(S)
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h(T)
          %h4#discussion Discussion
          %p
            Notice that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℋ
                    %mi H
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝒯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{H}_H \to \mathcal{T}
            in the above is nothing but the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibered+category"} fibered category
            that under the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+construction"} Grothendieck construction
            is an equivalent incarnation of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaf
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            in the above is assume to be just a 1-category of sets with structure,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℋ
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{H}_H
            is just its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+elements"} category of elements
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
          %p
            Similarly in all applications that arise in practice (for instance for the structure of
            = succeed "s)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒮
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝒯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S} \to \mathcal{T}
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibered+category"} fibered category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+construction"} Grothendieck construction
            to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prestack"} prestack
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mi 𝒮
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_{\mathcal{S}}
          %p
            Therefore morphisms of fibered categories over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                  %mo :
                  %mi 𝒮
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi ℋ
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  c : \mathcal{S} \to \mathcal{H}_H
          %p
            are equivalently morphisms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prestack"} (pre)
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stack"} stack
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi 𝒮
                  %mo →
                  %mi H
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  c : F_{\mathcal{S}} \to H
                  \\,.
          %p
            In either picture, these are morphism in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-topos"} 2-topos
            over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T}
          %p
            So, as before, for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi 𝒯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in \mathcal{T}
            some
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space"} space
            = succeed "-structure" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒮
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            (for instance a
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi 𝒮
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  g : X \to F_{\mathcal{S}}
          %p
            (in this setup simply by the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-Yoneda+lemma"} 2-Yoneda lemma
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [c(g)]
            of that bundle is the bullback of that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+characteristic+class"} universal class
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi g
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi 𝒮
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi c
                  %mi H
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  c(g) : X \stackrel{g}{\to} F_{\mathcal{S}} \stackrel{c}{\to} H
                  \\,.
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+differential+form"} characteristic differential form
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+characteristic+class"}> universal characteristic class
                ,
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+characteristic+map"} universal characteristic map
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+characteristic+class"} differential characteristic class
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+class+of+a+linear+representation"} characteristic class of a linear representation
          %h2#references References
          %p Textbook accounts include
          %ul
            %li#MilnorStasheff74
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Milnor"}> John Milnor
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Stasheff"} Jim Stasheff
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Characteristic classes
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://press.princeton.edu/books/paperback/9780691081229/characteristic-classes-am-76-volume-76"} ISBN:9780691081229
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1515/9781400881826"} doi:10.1515/9781400881826
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.maths.ed.ac.uk/~v1ranick/papers/milnstas.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://aareyanmanzoor.github.io/assets/books/characteristic-classes.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Kochmann96
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stanley+Kochmann"}> Stanley Kochmann
                , section 2.3 of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bordism%2C+Stable+Homotopy+and+Adams+Spectral+Sequences"} Bordism, Stable Homotopy and Adams Spectral Sequences
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dale+Husemoeller"}> Dale Husemoeller
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Joachim"} Michael Joachim
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Branislav+Jurco"} Branislav Jurco
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Schottenloher"} Martin Schottenloher
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Basic+Bundle+Theory+and+K-Cohomology+Invariants"} Basic Bundle Theory and K-Cohomology Invariants
              %p
                Lecture Notes in Physics, Springer 2008 (
                %a{:href => "http://www.mathematik.uni-muenchen.de/~schotten/Texte/978-3-540-74955-4_Book_LNP726corr1.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+May"}> Peter May
                , chapter 23 of
                %em A concise course in algebraic topology
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.uchicago.edu/~may/CONCISE/ConciseRevised.pdf"}> pdf
                )
          %p
            With an eye towards application in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematical+physics"} mathematical physics
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tohru+Eguchi"}> Tohru Eguchi
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Gilkey"} Peter Gilkey
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrew+Hanson"} Andrew Hanson
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Gravitation, gauge theories and differential geometry
                %strong 66
                6 (1980) 213-393 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0370-1573(80)90130-1"}> doi:10.1016/0370-1573(80)90130-1
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#Zhang11
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang+Zhang"}> Yang Zhang
                ,
                %em A brief introduction to characteristic classes from the differentiable viewpoint
                (2011) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://staff.ustc.edu.cn/~yzhphy/notes/A%20brief%20introduction%20to%20characteristic%20classes%20from%20the%20differentiable%20viewpoint.pdf"}> pdf
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Zhang_CharacteristicClasses.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mikio+Nakahara"}> Mikio Nakahara
                , Chapter 11 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Geometry%2C+Topology+and+Physics"} Geometry, Topology and Physics
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1201/9781315275826"} doi:10.1201/9781315275826
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://alpha.sinp.msu.ru/~panov/LibBooks/GRAV/(Graduate_Student_Series_in_Physics)Mikio_Nakahara-Geometry,_Topology_and_Physics,_Second_Edition_(Graduate_Student_Series_in_Physics)-Institute_of_Physics_Publishing(2003).pdf"} pdf
          %p Further texts include
          %ul#Fuks
            %li
              %p
                Jean-Pierre Schneiders,
                %em Introduction to characteristic classes and index theory
                (book), Lisboa (Lisbon) 2000
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Johan+Dupont"}> Johan Dupont
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Fibre bundles and Chern-Weil theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 69
                %a{:href => "https://data.math.au.dk/publications/ln/2003/imf-ln-2003-69.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                Shigeyuki Morita,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Geometry of characteristic classes
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 199
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Raoul+Bott"}> Raoul Bott
                , L. W. Tu,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Differential forms in algebraic topology
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 82
            %li
              %p
                D. B. Fuks,
                %em Непреривные когомологии топологических групп и характеристические классы
                , appendix to the Russian translation of K. S. Brown,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Cohomology of groups
